ating tools like Jsonnet is a plus. Kubernetes in Production: Skilled at diagnosing deployment failures, interpreting pod logs, and debugging scheduling issues and rollback scenarios in live environments. Understands how pods, ReplicaSets, and controllers interact in production. Programming & Code Analysis: Ability to read and debug code in Go and/or Ruby. Familiar with identifying performance issues, scalability concerns, and contributing to infrastructure tooling through thoughtful code analysis. Large Scale Operations Background: Experience supporting infrastructure for many customers or environments simultaneously. Comfortable managing isolation, scaling, monitoring, and incident response across diverse workloads. Architecture & Incident Response: Able to reason through complex systems and operational challenges. Brings on-call experience and can lead technical discussions and incident resolution efforts under pressure. Customer-Focused Collaboration: Proven ability to work across teams and with internal or external customers to solve technical problems while maintaining service commitments and clear communication. GitLab Platform Proficiency: Comfortable using GitLab as a daily tool for infrastructure automation, collaboration, and operational workflows. \n \n About the team GitLab\u2019s Dedicated team, where the SRE Environment Automation role sits, is on a mission to deliver a fully managed, single-tenant GitLab experience through the GitLab Dedicated platform. Our goal is to eliminate manual operations across the entire lifecycle of customer environments, including provisioning, upgrades, security, and monitoring, so customers can focus on unlocking the full potential of The One DevOps Platform without managing the underlying infrastructure. We build scalable, automated systems that ensure each GitLab Dedicated instance is secure, consistent, and production-ready\u2014whether we're managing 10 environments or hundreds. How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees \n \n Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being \n Flexible Paid Time Off\u00a0 \n Team Member Resource Groups \n Equity Compensation & Employee Stock Purchase Plan \n Growth and Development Fund \n Parental Leave \u00a0 \n \n Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from underrepresented groups are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you're excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application. \n \n Country Hiring Guidelines: GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.\u00a0\u00a0 \n Privacy Policy: Please review our Recruitment Privacy Policy. Your privacy is important to us. \n GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab\u2019s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also\u00a0 GitLab\u2019s EEO Policy \u00a0and\u00a0 EEO is the Law . If you have a disability or special need that requires\u00a0 accommodation , please let us know during the\u00a0 recruiting process . \nPlatforms Engineering\nIndia"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "The United States base range for this position is $132,948\u2013$189,927 USD, plus equity. The benefits available for this position include health insurance, six month paid parental leave, 401(k) retirement plan, monthly meal allowance, 23 paid days off, 13 paid flexible holidays, paid sick leave. These ranges may be modified in the future.\n\n\nSpotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n The United States base range for this position is $132,948\u2013$189,927 USD, plus equity. The benefits available for this position include health insurance, six month paid parental leave, 401(k) retirement plan, monthly meal allowance, 23 paid days off, 13 paid flexible holidays, paid sick leave. These ranges may be modified in the future. Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nPermanent\nEngineering\nNew York, NY\nPersonalization\nNew York, NY\nSpotify\u2019s Personalization Mission makes it easier for fans and artists to connect in more relevant and meaningful ways. We build the technology behind personalized experiences across Spotify, helping listeners discover and engage with the content they love.\n\nWe\u2019re looking for a Backend Engineer to join a team within our Personalization organization that builds foundational backend infrastructure powering recommendations across Spotify. Our systems help teams efficiently identify, retrieve, rank, and filter relevant content to create personalized experiences for millions of listeners around the world.\n\nThe team works on large-scale systems that support content and user representations, candidate generation, and centralized filtering for recommendations. Our technology is used across many of Spotify\u2019s user-facing experiences, giving you the opportunity to solve complex backend challenges with broad impact across the product.\n\n Spotify\u2019s Personalization Mission makes it easier for fans and artists to connect in more relevant and meaningful ways. We build the technology behind personalized experiences across Spotify, helping listeners discover and engage with the content they love. \n We\u2019re looking for a Backend Engineer to join a team within our Personalization organization that builds foundational backend infrastructure powering recommendations across Spotify. Our systems help teams efficiently identify, retrieve, rank, and filter relevant content to create personalized experiences for millions of listeners around the world. \n The team works on large-scale systems that support content and user representations, candidate generation, and centralized filtering for recommendations. Our technology is used across many of Spotify\u2019s user-facing experiences, giving you the opportunity to solve complex backend challenges with broad impact across the product. \n318f73b5-6a78-49c7-b625-ecb1481042b9\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n Build, maintain, and evolve backend systems that support personalization and recommendations at Spotify scale. \n Develop infrastructure that enables efficient retrieval, ranking, and filtering of personalized content. \n Build platform capabilities that support candidate generation and representations of content and users. \n Design reliable, scalable, and performant services capable of supporting high-volume recommendation workloads. \n Partner with engineers and teams across Spotify to understand their needs and build reusable platform solutions. \n Improve the reliability, observability, maintainability, and operational performance of the systems the team owns. \n Participate in technical design discussions and contribute to architectural decisions as our platforms continue to evolve. \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n You have professional experience building and operating backend systems in production. \n You have experience with distributed systems, APIs, data-intensive applications, or large-scale service architectures. \n You\u2019re comfortable working with systems where reliability, latency, and scalability matter. \n You can independently own engineering projects while collaborating effectively with engineers across teams. \n You\u2019re interested in the infrastructure behind recommendation and personalization systems; prior machine learning experience is helpful but not required. \n You enjoy solving platform-level problems and building systems that other engineering teams depend on. \n You care about writing maintainable code, making thoughtful technical decisions, and continuously improving production systems. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n We are a distributed workforce enabling our band members to find a work mode that is best for them! \n Where in the world? For this role, it can be anywhere in the North America region in which we have a work location \n Prefer to work in an office environment? Prefer to work from home instead? Not a problem! We have plenty of options for your working preferences. Find more information about our Work From Anywhere options here. \n Working hours? We operate within the Eastern Standard time zone for collaboration. \n\n \nBackend Engineer, Personalization\nUS\nremote\n\n\n Spotify\u2019s Personalization Mission makes it easier for fans and artists to connect in more relevant and meaningful ways. We build the technology behind personalized experiences across Spotify, helping listeners discover and engage with the content they love. \n We\u2019re looking for a Backend Engineer to join a team within our Personalization organization that builds foundational backend infrastructure powering recommendations across Spotify. Our systems help teams efficiently identify, retrieve, rank, and filter relevant content to create personalized experiences for millions of listeners around the world. \n The team works on large-scale systems that support content and user representations, candidate generation, and centralized filtering for recommendations. Our technology is used across many of Spotify\u2019s user-facing experiences, giving you the opportunity to solve complex backend challenges with broad impact across the product. \nSpotify\u2019s Personalization Mission makes it easier for fans and artists to connect in more relevant and meaningful ways. We build the technology behind personalized experiences across Spotify, helping listeners discover and engage with the content they love.\n\nWe\u2019re looking for a Backend Engineer to join a team within our Personalization organization that builds foundational backend infrastructure powering recommendations across Spotify. Our systems help teams efficiently identify, retrieve, rank, and filter relevant content to create personalized experiences for millions of listeners around the world.\n\nThe team works on large-scale systems that support content and user representations, candidate generation, and centralized filtering for recommendations. Our technology is used across many of Spotify\u2019s user-facing experiences, giving you the opportunity to solve complex backend challenges with broad impact across the product.\n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/318f73b5-6a78-49c7-b625-ecb1481042b9\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/318f73b5-6a78-49c7-b625-ecb1481042b9/apply"}, "return": {"value": 132948, "stated": true, "evidence": "$132,948\u2013$189,927"}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\n Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \nPermanent\nAdvertising\nLondon\nAdvertising Sales - Emerging and Scaled Sales\nLondon\nSell what you love. For us and millions of users across the globe, that\u2019s Spotify. Join the Sales team and you\u2019ll build the relationships that help grow our business in existing markets and beyond. We don\u2019t just sell creative solutions to our clients and partners, we help to shape them; using our expert knowledge of ad products, sales channels and the industry to impact the way the world experiences music and podcasts.\u00a0\n\n\nWe are looking for an exceptional Client Partner to join our Emerging & Scaled team, one of the fastest-growing units within Spotify\u2019s Ad Sales organization. This role is perfect for someone who wakes up every morning excited to connect with clients and inspire them with the power of Spotify.\u00a0\nYou bring curiosity, resilience, and a collaborative mindset, along with a passion for building meaningful client partnerships. Integrity and a healthy work-life balance are non-negotiable. You\u2019ll shape how Spotify advertisers reach audiences and elevate their connection to our platform.\n\n Sell what you love. For us and millions of users across the globe, that\u2019s Spotify. Join the Sales team and you\u2019ll build the relationships that help grow our business in existing markets and beyond. We don\u2019t just sell creative solutions to our clients and partners, we help to shape them; using our expert knowledge of ad products, sales channels and the industry to impact the way the world experiences music and podcasts.\u00a0 \n We are looking for an exceptional Client Partner to join our Emerging & Scaled team, one of the fastest-growing units within Spotify's Ad Sales organisation. This role is oriented to building and growing Spotify's relationships with UK Independent Agencies. This role is perfect for someone who wakes up every morning excited to connect with clients and inspire them with the power of Spotify.\u00a0 \n You bring curiosity, resilience, and a collaborative mindset, along with a passion for building meaningful client partnerships. Integrity and a healthy work-life balance are non-negotiable. You\u2019ll shape how Spotify agencies and advertisers reach audiences and elevate their connection to our platform.\u00a0 \n \u00a0 \n \n35e07377-d8a5-47b4-b3f1-c443de3c86dd\nWhat You\u2019ll Do\n\n Client Strategy: Lead consultative selling to inspire clients and demonstrate how Spotify can achieve their business goals. \n Business Development: Proactively identify and cultivate high-potential customer relationships across diverse verticals to grow a robust sales pipeline. \n Agency Partnerships: Build deep, trusted partnerships with indie agency leaders, becoming their go-to expert on audio and digital advertising through Spotify. \n Sales Propositions: Craft and present effective sales propositions, leveraging the latest platform innovations, research, and key insights. \n Sales Targets: Own and exceed ambitious revenue goals through strategic, entrepreneurial approaches that drive sustainable growth. \n Strategic Insight & Reporting: Deliver actionable insights and detailed performance reports, analyzing campaigns to recommend improvements. \n Product Expertise: Stay ahead of Spotify\u2019s product innovations, identifying cross-selling opportunities to help clients succeed. \n Pipeline Development: Skillfully manage multiple complex conversations, prioritizing engagements with efficiency using relevant software tools. \n Cross-Functional Collaboration: Collaborate with Product, Marketing, and Data teams to create comprehensive strategies and optimize platform effectiveness. \n\nWho You Are\n\n Knowledgeable: You bring a minimum of 5+ years of experience managing pipelines and driving revenue in a digital advertising tech environment. Experience in audio advertising is a plus. \n Market and Segment Expertise: You have a strong understanding of the UK advertising, media, and ad tech landscape - particularly the independent agency ecosystem. You know what makes indies tick and how they differ from network agencies. \n Relationship Builder: You have a proven track record of developing and maintaining strong partnerships with agencies, understanding their unique needs, structures, and decision-making processes. \n Organized & Self-Reliant: You thrive in a fast-paced environment and can manage multiple priorities with confidence \n Articulate: You are an effective communicator, clearly expressing both your stakeholders\u2019 needs and your own. \n Intrinsically Motivated: You are driven by your own goals and always aim to beat your personal best. \n Results Oriented: You thrive on exceeding targets and making a tangible impact. \n Team-Oriented: You believe in collaborative success, eager to learn from your peers and share your expertise. \n English language fluency, spoken and written is required. \n Please apply with a CV in English. \n\nWhere You\u2019ll Be\n\n This role is based in London. \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. We ask that you come in 2-3 times per week. \n\nClient Partner - Emerging & Scaled, Independent Agency (UK)\nGB\nhybrid\n Sell what you love. For us and millions of users across the globe, that\u2019s Spotify. Join the Sales team and you\u2019ll build the relationships that help grow our business in existing markets and beyond. We don\u2019t just sell creative solutions to our clients and partners, we help to shape them; using our expert knowledge of ad products, sales channels and the industry to impact the way the world experiences music and podcasts.\u00a0 \nSell what you love. For us and millions of users across the globe, that\u2019s Spotify. Join the Sales team and you\u2019ll build the relationships that help grow our business in existing markets and beyond. We don\u2019t just sell creative solutions to our clients and partners, we help to shape them; using our expert knowledge of ad products, sales channels and the industry to impact the way the world experiences music and podcasts.\u00a0\n\n \n We are looking for an exceptional Client Partner to join our Emerging & Scaled team, one of the fastest-growing units within Spotify's Ad Sales organisation. This role is oriented to building and growing Spotify's relationships with UK Independent Agencies. This role is perfect for someone who wakes up every morning excited to connect with clients and inspire them with the power of Spotify.\u00a0 \n You bring curiosity, resilience, and a collaborative mindset, along with a passion for building meaningful client partnerships. Integrity and a healthy work-life balance are non-negotiable. You\u2019ll shape how Spotify agencies and advertisers reach audiences and elevate their connection to our platform.\u00a0 \n \u00a0 \n \nWe are looking for an exceptional Client Partner to join our Emerging & Scaled team, one of the fastest-growing units within Spotify\u2019s Ad Sales organization. This role is perfect for someone who wakes up every morning excited to connect with clients and inspire them with the power of Spotify.\u00a0\nYou bring curiosity, resilience, and a collaborative mindset, along with a passion for building meaningful client partnerships. Integrity and a healthy work-life balance are non-negotiable. You\u2019ll shape how Spotify advertisers reach audiences and elevate their connection to our platform.\n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/35e07377-d8a5-47b4-b3f1-c443de3c86dd\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/35e07377-d8a5-47b4-b3f1-c443de3c86dd/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "The United States base range for this position is $229,874\u2013$328,392 USD, plus equity. The benefits available for this position include health insurance, six-month paid parental leave, 401(k) retirement plan, monthly meal allowance, 23 paid days off, paid flexible holidays, and paid sick leave. These ranges may be modified in the future. \nPermanent\nProduct\nNew York, NY\nMusic\nNew York, NY\n\n \n The Music Mission team owns Spotify\u2019s end to end proposition for music creators and the experiences they create for fans. The team is dedicated to building tools and services to enable creation, promotion, expression, and monetization at scale. \n The Music team shapes how artists and their music show up on Spotify. Our work spans Spotify for Artists, content upload, artist identity and visual expression, promotion and discovery, and insights that help artists and their teams understand and grow their audiences. \n As Head of Artist & Label Product, you\u2019ll lead the product organization responsible for these experiences, bringing together our artist and label products into a clear, connected strategy. You\u2019ll lead PM managers and senior PMs, set direction across multiple product areas, and turn that strategy into meaningful outcomes for artists, labels, listeners, and Spotify. You\u2019ll report to the VP of Product, Design and Insights for the Music Vertical and be a key member of the extended Music leadership team. \n \u00a0 \n \ne2c7bbb8-f873-42c7-811f-0bd45bf452ae\nWhat You'll Do \n \n\n Set the strategy and direction for Spotify\u2019s artist and label products, connecting artist tools, promotion, discovery, expression, and insights into a coherent product experience. \n Own business and product outcomes across the portfolio, translating long-term strategy into clear priorities and near-term goals. \n Lead, coach, and develop PM managers and senior PMs, creating an environment where people can do their best work and continue strengthening their product craft. \n Advance how the product organization uses AI to improve the way we build, learn, make decisions, and deliver value. \n Make thoughtful prioritization and resource decisions across product areas, navigating trade-offs and keeping teams focused on the outcomes that matter most. \n Partner closely with Design, Engineering, Product Insights, Content, and Business leaders to build high-quality products at Spotify\u2019s scale. \n Represent the needs of artists and labels in key product and business decisions, helping teams balance creator, listener, and Spotify priorities. \n Navigate a complex music ecosystem, including relationships with labels and distributors, legal and licensing considerations, and dependencies across Spotify. \n\n \nWho You Are \n \n\n You bring 12+ years of product management experience, including 5+ years leading product managers and product management leaders. \n You have led complex product portfolios and can turn broad opportunities into clear strategies, priorities, and measurable outcomes. \n You have experience building products for multi-sided platforms and understand how to create value for different groups with distinct needs. \n You understand the commercial side of product development and are comfortable working across revenue, engagement, and user-experience goals. \n You have experience creating new products and scaling established products to serve large audiences. \n You can move comfortably between long-term strategy and detailed product decisions, communicating effectively with senior leaders while staying close to teams and customers. \n You build trusted cross-functional relationships and have delivered complex products across teams, disciplines, and organizational boundaries. \n You communicate complex ideas clearly and create frameworks that help teams make informed decisions and move forward. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be \n \n\n This role is based in New York \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nHead of Product Management - Artist Products\nUS\nremote\n\n\n \n The Music Mission team owns Spotify\u2019s end to end proposition for music creators and the experiences they create for fans. The team is dedicated to building tools and services to enable creation, promotion, expression, and monetization at scale. \n The Music team shapes how artists and their music show up on Spotify. Our work spans Spotify for Artists, content upload, artist identity and visual expression, promotion and discovery, and insights that help artists and their teams understand and grow their audiences. \n As Head of Artist & Label Product, you\u2019ll lead the product organization responsible for these experiences, bringing together our artist and label products into a clear, connected strategy. You\u2019ll lead PM managers and senior PMs, set direction across multiple product areas, and turn that strategy into meaningful outcomes for artists, labels, listeners, and Spotify. You\u2019ll report to the VP of Product, Design and Insights for the Music Vertical and be a key member of the extended Music leadership team. \n \u00a0 \n \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/e2c7bbb8-f873-42c7-811f-0bd45bf452ae\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/e2c7bbb8-f873-42c7-811f-0bd45bf452ae/apply"}, "return": {"value": 229874, "stated": true, "evidence": "$229,874"}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Permanent\nContent\nParis\nMusic Business\nParis\nWe are looking for a strategic-minded, execution-oriented Artist & Label Partnerships Manager for France, to join Spotify\u2019s Music team based in Paris. In this role, you will sit at the heart of the music ecosystem, moving between high-level release strategies and the day-to-day tactical execution that drives artist and business growth. This role is perfect for a music industry professional who thrives on building relationships and navigating the intersection of technology and creativity.\n\u00a0\nOur ideal candidate has fun at work and a desire to make a positive impact on the music industry as a whole. Above all, your work will impact the way the world experiences music and strengthen Spotify\u2019s role as a trusted, culturally relevant voice in the music landscape.\u00a0\n\u00a0\n\n \n We are looking for a strategic-minded, execution-oriented Artist & Label Partnerships Manager for France, to join Spotify\u2019s Music team based in Paris. In this role, you will sit at the heart of the music ecosystem, moving between high-level release strategies and the day-to-day tactical execution that drives artist and business growth. This role is perfect for a music industry professional who thrives on building relationships and navigating the intersection of technology and creativity. \n \u00a0 \n Our ideal candidate has fun at work and a desire to make a positive impact on the music industry as a whole. Above all, your work will impact the way the world experiences music and strengthen Spotify\u2019s role as a trusted, culturally relevant voice in the music landscape.\u00a0 \n \u00a0 \n \nd06fe312-4b91-4c40-a3da-64985b569075\nWhat You'll do \n \u00a0 \n\n Focusing on the French music landscape, you will be the primary point of contact for local music partners based in France, ensuring that Spotify remains the most valued partner for artists and our industry partners, utilising on-platform promotion and off-platform initiatives to ensure Spotify is the premiere platform for artist development \n Support and educate our key partners across artists and labels communities in France on Spotify tools, resources and insights to encourage them and improve their daily business \n You will contribute your expertise to various music-related projects within the company, executing on creative and cross-functional collaborations in the region and beyond, building impactful and innovative artist partnerships to enable artists development and artist-fan engagement \n You will proactively identify music trends, emerging talent and opportunities in the local and global music landscape, providing deep cultural and musical insights with the local FR team to execute pivotal initiatives, multi-market campaigns and other key internal partners & teams including editorial, consumer marketing, communications, strategy & operations\u2026 \n Lead artist & label partnerships representation in high-impact cross-functional projects and strategic bets \n Ensure Spotify has the best possible content offering in France and use this to further Spotify's appeal to existing and new users \n Connect other Spotify teams with the music industry to help drive and execute opportunities driven by Spotify and our partners. You will act as liaison between Spotify and artist / label partners. \n\nWho You Are \n \n\n You have significant experience with label and artist relations in an established digital music service, record label, media or tech company.\u00a0 \n You have a deep understanding and established network within the local music industry in France and have built relevant contacts with labels and artists to effectively collaborate with the community \n You will demonstrate a team player spirit, a passion for performance-oriented analytics, and a solid understanding of Spotify's role in the music industry both locally and globally \n You are skilled at leveraging data and audience insights to support strategic decisions and build clear narratives \n You are culturally aware, with the ability to critically evaluate music trends, emerging movements and audience behaviour beyond just data \n You have excellent negotiating, presentation and people skills. You are able to prepare and deliver executive level presentations, effectively advocate for the market and secure stakeholder buy-in with ease \n You are well organised and detail-oriented with the ability to plan, deliver on tight deadlines and pay outstanding attention to detail \n You are at ease and have proven experience navigating fast-changing priorities in a dynamic environment, comfortable navigating complex global-to-local organizational structures and aligning cross-functional teams around Music priorities \n You have strong project management skills with a consistent record in marketing and operations, and feel at ease with digital and AI tools \n You possess a perfect level of written and spoken English\u00a0 \n Finally, you're a great teammate and always have a positive and humble attitude. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n For this role, the preferred locations is Paris.\u00a0 \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! We ask that you come in 2-3 times per week. \n\n \nManager, Artists Label & Partnerships\nFR\nhybrid\n\n\n \n We are looking for a strategic-minded, execution-oriented Artist & Label Partnerships Manager for France, to join Spotify\u2019s Music team based in Paris. In this role, you will sit at the heart of the music ecosystem, moving between high-level release strategies and the day-to-day tactical execution that drives artist and business growth. This role is perfect for a music industry professional who thrives on building relationships and navigating the intersection of technology and creativity. \n \u00a0 \n Our ideal candidate has fun at work and a desire to make a positive impact on the music industry as a whole. Above all, your work will impact the way the world experiences music and strengthen Spotify\u2019s role as a trusted, culturally relevant voice in the music landscape.\u00a0 \n \u00a0 \n \nWe are looking for a strategic-minded, execution-oriented Artist & Label Partnerships Manager for France, to join Spotify\u2019s Music team based in Paris. In this role, you will sit at the heart of the music ecosystem, moving between high-level release strategies and the day-to-day tactical execution that drives artist and business growth. This role is perfect for a music industry professional who thrives on building relationships and navigating the intersection of technology and creativity.\n\u00a0\nOur ideal candidate has fun at work and a desire to make a positive impact on the music industry as a whole. Above all, your work will impact the way the world experiences music and strengthen Spotify\u2019s role as a trusted, culturally relevant voice in the music landscape.\u00a0\n\u00a0\n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/d06fe312-4b91-4c40-a3da-64985b569075\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/d06fe312-4b91-4c40-a3da-64985b569075/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Permanent\nProduct\nStockholm\nExperience\nStockholm\nLondon\nWe design Spotify\u2019s consumer experience\u2014end to end, moment to moment, across every screen, platform, and partner integration. Our mission is to make listening feel effortless, personal, and joyful for billions of users around the world. That means turning complexity into clarity across hundreds of touchpoints\u2014from our mobile and desktop apps to the smart speakers, TVs, cars, and integrations where Spotify shows up every day. If it touches a consumer, we shape it. We bring deep insight into human behavior, design, and technology to craft experiences that feel intuitive, expressive, and unmistakably Spotify.\nWe are looking for a Principal Product Manager who will join the Play Product Area within the Core Experience Studio to help evolve the experience of audio and media playback on Spotify. You will help define and evolve the experiences that make playing on Spotify more engaging, rewarding, and valuable for users, creators, and Spotify. Above all, your work will impact how hundreds of millions users experience music and media.\n\n \n We design Spotify\u2019s consumer experience\u2014end to end, moment to moment, across every screen, platform, and partner integration. Our mission is to make listening feel effortless, personal, and joyful for billions of users around the world. That means turning complexity into clarity across hundreds of touchpoints\u2014from our mobile and desktop apps to the smart speakers, TVs, cars, and integrations where Spotify shows up every day. If it touches a consumer, we shape it. We bring deep insight into human behavior, design, and technology to craft experiences that feel intuitive, expressive, and unmistakably Spotify. \n We are looking for a Principal Product Manager who will join the Play Product Area within the Core Experience Studio to help evolve the experience of audio and media playback on Spotify. You will help define and evolve the experiences that make playing on Spotify more engaging, rewarding, and valuable for users, creators, and Spotify. Above all, your work will impact how hundreds of millions users experience music and media. \n \n080868dd-fc8c-4648-b6ab-6780d8ca3d63\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n \n Work with a cross-functional team that looks after our audio playback capabilities \n \n \n Work with engineering, design, data science and user research to ensure the experience is scalable, usable, and useful for a range of strategies \n \n \n Lead multiple projects across the entire product lifecycle \n \n \n Triangulate data and insights to develop a robust product strategy and inform decision-making as well as short- and long-term roadmaps \n \n \n Manage cross-functional and cross-org relationships to keep teams and leaders informed, receive input, and influence their thinking \n \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n \n You are an experienced product manager with the ability to work with cross-functional teams, lead complex projects across multiple strategies and stakeholders, and make data-driven decisions \n \n \n You are an expert in audio experiences, with a strong understanding of both the engineering aspects of audio processing and editing, as well as their impact on the user listening experience. For example, you understand how features like crossfading and beatmatching influence the flow and feel of an audio session, while also ensuring high overall audio quality \n \n \n Experience from developing video playback experiences (in addition to audio) is a plus; e.g. low-latency video delivery, DRM, and optimizing playback for improved QoE \n \n \n You have led the product work of several products in large tech companies that you can tell us about \n \n \n You have a deep understanding of product practices and know how to incorporate multiple different perspectives (including user research, data and strategy) into one single product vision and experience \n \n \n You care about creating engaging, rewarding, and valuable experiences for users, creators, and Spotify \n \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n This role is based in Stockholm or London. \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nPrincipal Product Manager - Audio and Media Playback\nSE\nhybrid\n\n\n \n We design Spotify\u2019s consumer experience\u2014end to end, moment to moment, across every screen, platform, and partner integration. Our mission is to make listening feel effortless, personal, and joyful for billions of users around the world. That means turning complexity into clarity across hundreds of touchpoints\u2014from our mobile and desktop apps to the smart speakers, TVs, cars, and integrations where Spotify shows up every day. If it touches a consumer, we shape it. We bring deep insight into human behavior, design, and technology to craft experiences that feel intuitive, expressive, and unmistakably Spotify. \n We are looking for a Principal Product Manager who will join the Play Product Area within the Core Experience Studio to help evolve the experience of audio and media playback on Spotify. You will help define and evolve the experiences that make playing on Spotify more engaging, rewarding, and valuable for users, creators, and Spotify. Above all, your work will impact how hundreds of millions users experience music and media. \n \nWe design Spotify\u2019s consumer experience\u2014end to end, moment to moment, across every screen, platform, and partner integration. Our mission is to make listening feel effortless, personal, and joyful for billions of users around the world. That means turning complexity into clarity across hundreds of touchpoints\u2014from our mobile and desktop apps to the smart speakers, TVs, cars, and integrations where Spotify shows up every day. If it touches a consumer, we shape it. We bring deep insight into human behavior, design, and technology to craft experiences that feel intuitive, expressive, and unmistakably Spotify.\nWe are looking for a Principal Product Manager who will join the Play Product Area within the Core Experience Studio to help evolve the experience of audio and media playback on Spotify. You will help define and evolve the experiences that make playing on Spotify more engaging, rewarding, and valuable for users, creators, and Spotify. Above all, your work will impact how hundreds of millions users experience music and media.\n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/080868dd-fc8c-4648-b6ab-6780d8ca3d63\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/080868dd-fc8c-4648-b6ab-6780d8ca3d63/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n \n \n The United States base range for this position is $133,194 - $190,278 plus equity. The benefits available for this position include health insurance, six month paid parental leave, 401(k) retirement plan, a monthly meal allowance, 23 paid days off, 13 paid flexible holidays. These ranges may be modified in the future. \n \n Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nPermanent\nData and Analytics\nNew York, NY\nPersonalization\nNew York, NY\n\n The Personalization team makes deciding what to play next easier and more enjoyable for every listener. From Blend to Discover Weekly, we\u2019re behind some of Spotify\u2019s most-loved features. We built them by understanding the world of music and podcasts better than anyone else. Join us and you\u2019ll keep millions of users listening by making great recommendations to each and every one of them.Spotify\u2019s \n \u00a0 \n Personalization organization builds the technology that helps millions of listeners discover what they love. Within this space, our research team focuses on advancing the state of the art in machine learning and AI to shape the future of personalization. We explore new approaches, challenge existing assumptions, and contribute to the broader research community while influencing long-term product direction. \n9e3bdb48-67eb-49d9-ae0b-a337ba69a05f\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n Conduct original research in machine learning and AI, with a focus on large-scale foundation models, generative AI, and post-training methods, including reinforcement learning. \n Develop novel methodologies, models, and evaluation frameworks to advance personalization systems. \n Design and execute rigorous experiments to explore new ideas and validate research hypotheses. \n Contribute to the scientific community through publications, talks, and conference participation. \n Collaborate with cross-functional partners to translate research insights into long-term product opportunities. \n Help define and evolve a forward-looking research agenda aligned with Spotify\u2019s personalization strategy. \n Mentor others and contribute to a strong, curious, and collaborative research culture. \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n You have a Master\u2019s or PhD in machine learning, AI, or a related field, or equivalent research experience. \n You have demonstrated expertise in machine learning and artificial intelligence through peer-reviewed publications at conferences such as NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, KDD, or RecSys. \n You have deep knowledge of machine learning, with hands-on experience in areas such as post-training and reinforcement learning for large models, reward design, large-scale distributed training, or evaluation of model behavior. \n You are experienced in designing experiments and working with real-world datasets to validate research ideas. \n You care about advancing understanding of user behavior and improving experiences across music and talk content. \n You bring curiosity, creativity, and a thoughtful approach to solving complex, open-ended problems. \n You value collaboration and actively seek diverse perspectives in your work. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n This role is based in New York City. \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nResearch Scientist - Personalization\nUS\nremote\n\n\n The Personalization team makes deciding what to play next easier and more enjoyable for every listener. From Blend to Discover Weekly, we\u2019re behind some of Spotify\u2019s most-loved features. We built them by understanding the world of music and podcasts better than anyone else. Join us and you\u2019ll keep millions of users listening by making great recommendations to each and every one of them.Spotify\u2019s \n \u00a0 \n Personalization organization builds the technology that helps millions of listeners discover what they love. Within this space, our research team focuses on advancing the state of the art in machine learning and AI to shape the future of personalization. We explore new approaches, challenge existing assumptions, and contribute to the broader research community while influencing long-term product direction. \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/9e3bdb48-67eb-49d9-ae0b-a337ba69a05f\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/9e3bdb48-67eb-49d9-ae0b-a337ba69a05f/apply"}, "return": {"value": 133194, "stated": true, "evidence": "$133,194 - $190,278"}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nPermanent\nData and Analytics\nLondon\nPersonalization\nLondon\nStockholm\n\n \n he Personalization team makes deciding what to play next easier and more enjoyable for every listener. From Blend to Discover Weekly, we're behind some of Spotify's most-loved features. We built them by understanding the world of music and podcasts better than anyone else. Join us and you'll keep millions of users listening by making great recommendations to each and every one of them. \n Within Personalization, the Speak Team owns the development of Spotify's state-of-the-art speech models, contributing to speech recognition, speech synthesis, and speech-to-speech models. We craft voice models that match human-level emotional expressiveness, so we can deeply engage our listeners and support creators at scale. Our groundbreaking work on speech synthesis relies on state-of-the-art deep learning methods and evaluation techniques, highly efficient data processing and model serving, and capturing audio of outstanding quality from our voice talent pool. \n We're looking for a senior applied research scientist with experience in developing novel ML techniques and architectures and with a strong interest in working across a full production pipeline to produce state-of-the-art generative conversational speech-to-speech models. You'll collaborate with our engineering teams to help develop our production pipelines, explore new ideas and methods to improve quality, understanding and realism, as well as push the frontiers of what is possible with our speech technology. \n \na4c49acb-a095-4452-ad9e-69e4b778c256\nWhat You'll Do\n \n \n\n Develop and experiment with new methods for speech synthesis and speech recognition, along with end-to-end approaches, building on the latest research and ideas. \n Work towards the expansion of our speech use-cases targeting different markets and products. \n Be part of a highly motivated research team dedicated to building and creating models at scale to power the Spotify platform. \n Champion best practices for research and development, sharing your knowledge and experience with other researchers within Speak. \n Collaborate with our engineering and data teams on ideas requiring new infrastructure or new high-quality data, as well as to help improve our speech recognition and speech synthesis pipelines, and help turn proven ideas into scalable products. \n\n \n \nWho You Are\n \n \n\n You have a strong background in ML (PhD degree on top of professional experience), and \n experience in working with any of the following: transformers, GANs, diffusion models, flow matching, VAEs, audio codecs. \n You have experience in developing generative models for speech synthesis, speech recognition, audio/music, natural language processing, or computer vision. \n You have strong experience with Python, particularly PyTorch. \n You have strong communication skills and the ability to explain technical ideas with clarity to technical and non-technical people alike. \n You have experience in an academic or professional setting conducting high-quality research. \n\n \n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n \n\n This role is based in London or Stockholm. \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home \n\n \n \nSenior Applied Research Scientist - Personalization\nGB\nremote\n\n\n \n he Personalization team makes deciding what to play next easier and more enjoyable for every listener. From Blend to Discover Weekly, we're behind some of Spotify's most-loved features. We built them by understanding the world of music and podcasts better than anyone else. Join us and you'll keep millions of users listening by making great recommendations to each and every one of them. \n Within Personalization, the Speak Team owns the development of Spotify's state-of-the-art speech models, contributing to speech recognition, speech synthesis, and speech-to-speech models. We craft voice models that match human-level emotional expressiveness, so we can deeply engage our listeners and support creators at scale. Our groundbreaking work on speech synthesis relies on state-of-the-art deep learning methods and evaluation techniques, highly efficient data processing and model serving, and capturing audio of outstanding quality from our voice talent pool. \n We're looking for a senior applied research scientist with experience in developing novel ML techniques and architectures and with a strong interest in working across a full production pipeline to produce state-of-the-art generative conversational speech-to-speech models. You'll collaborate with our engineering teams to help develop our production pipelines, explore new ideas and methods to improve quality, understanding and realism, as well as push the frontiers of what is possible with our speech technology. \n \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/a4c49acb-a095-4452-ad9e-69e4b778c256\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/a4c49acb-a095-4452-ad9e-69e4b778c256/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n The United States base range for this position is $87,000 \u2013 $125,000 USD, plus equity. The benefits available for this position include health insurance, six-month paid parental leave, 401(k) retirement plan, monthly meal allowance, 23 paid days off, paid flexible holidays, and paid sick leave. These ranges may be modified in the future. Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nPermanent\nPeople\nNew York, NY\nHuman Resources\nNew York, NY\n\n \n We\u2019re looking for a Senior Digital Learning Experience Designer to join our Learning & Inclusion team, the group responsible for creating learning experiences that help every Spotify band member grow, belong, and do their best work. \n You\u2019ll bring together instructional design, visual design, storytelling, and broader learning and development expertise to create inclusive and effective experiences at scale. You\u2019ll partner with subject-matter experts, people leaders, and Learning & Inclusion colleagues on company-wide initiatives, from leadership development to programs that bring Spotify\u2019s values to life. \n \n9d1c90b5-a8a4-4218-b2f3-7bbaefae7fd1\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n Lead the end-to-end design of learning experiences, from needs analysis and curriculum architecture through development, launch, and evaluation. \n Partner with subject-matter experts and stakeholders to identify performance needs and turn them into clear learning objectives and practical solutions. \n Design learning journeys across live, digital, blended, and self-directed formats using evidence-based learning principles. \n Create engaging learning materials, including eLearning, facilitator guides, participant resources, job aids, presentations, and micro-learning experiences. \n Use visual design and storytelling to make complex ideas clear, memorable, and engaging while creating experiences that feel unmistakably Spotify. \n Build interactive digital learning experiences using AI-assisted workflows and authoring tools such as Articulate Storyline or Rise, Adobe Captivate, or similar platforms. \n Design inclusive learning experiences that reflect different perspectives, reduce barriers to participation, and support a culture of belonging. \n Pilot and iterate on learning experiences using learner feedback, stakeholder input, and performance data. \n Define meaningful measures of success and evaluate learning effectiveness, knowledge transfer, learner experience, and behavior change. \n Manage multiple learning projects from initial scoping through delivery while creating clarity around priorities, timelines, and stakeholder expectations. \n Explore emerging approaches in learning design, including AI-assisted authoring and adaptive learning, and apply them where they can meaningfully improve the learner experience. \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n You have 5+ years of professional instructional design experience and a portfolio demonstrating thoughtful work across multiple learning formats. \n You apply learning science principles such as cognitive load, retrieval practice, spaced learning, and adult learning theory to practical design decisions. \n You know how to uncover learning and performance needs, translate them into measurable objectives, and design learning journeys that build knowledge and skills over time. \n You create meaningful practice through scenarios, simulations, assessments, and other interactive experiences rather than relying on passive content. \n You have strong visual and UX design judgment and understand how typography, hierarchy, layout, and visual storytelling can make learning clearer and easier to navigate. \n You have experience with rapid authoring tools such as Articulate 360, Captivate, Lectora, or similar platforms, along with design tools such as Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, or equivalent. \n You can create clear storyboards, scripts, facilitator guides, and supporting materials that help others confidently deliver consistent learning experiences. \n You use learner feedback and data to evaluate effectiveness, iterate on your work, and connect learning experiences to meaningful outcomes. \n You communicate complex ideas clearly and collaborate effectively with subject-matter experts, leaders, and cross-functional partners. \n You\u2019re comfortable navigating ambiguity, balancing multiple priorities, and taking ownership from an early idea through a polished learning experience. \n You bring experience in areas such as inclusive learning design, leadership development, learning technology, short-form learning video or animation, LMS/LXP platforms, or SCORM/xAPI. \n You have a degree in instructional design, learning sciences, education, human-computer interaction, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n This role is based in New York \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nSenior Digital Learning Experience Designer - Learning & Inclusion\nUS\nhybrid\n\n\n \n We\u2019re looking for a Senior Digital Learning Experience Designer to join our Learning & Inclusion team, the group responsible for creating learning experiences that help every Spotify band member grow, belong, and do their best work. \n You\u2019ll bring together instructional design, visual design, storytelling, and broader learning and development expertise to create inclusive and effective experiences at scale. You\u2019ll partner with subject-matter experts, people leaders, and Learning & Inclusion colleagues on company-wide initiatives, from leadership development to programs that bring Spotify\u2019s values to life. \n \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/9d1c90b5-a8a4-4218-b2f3-7bbaefae7fd1\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/9d1c90b5-a8a4-4218-b2f3-7bbaefae7fd1/apply"}, "return": {"value": 87000, "stated": true, "evidence": "$87,000 \u2013 $125,000 USD"}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nPermanent\nPeople\nLondon\nHuman Resources\nLondon\nStockholm\n\n \n We\u2019re looking for a Senior Digital Learning Experience Designer to join our Learning & Inclusion team, the group responsible for creating learning experiences that help every Spotify band member grow, belong, and do their best work. \n You\u2019ll bring together instructional design, visual design, storytelling, and broader learning and development expertise to create inclusive and effective experiences at scale. You\u2019ll partner with subject-matter experts, people leaders, and Learning & Inclusion colleagues on company-wide initiatives, from leadership development to programs that bring Spotify\u2019s values to life. \n \n7cf725bb-99c8-4717-b7e5-4f4708fa4169\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n Lead the end-to-end design of learning experiences, from needs analysis and curriculum architecture through development, launch, and evaluation. \n Partner with subject-matter experts and stakeholders to identify performance needs and turn them into clear learning objectives and practical solutions. \n Design learning journeys across live, digital, blended, and self-directed formats using evidence-based learning principles. \n Create engaging learning materials, including eLearning, facilitator guides, participant resources, job aids, presentations, and micro-learning experiences. \n Use visual design and storytelling to make complex ideas clear, memorable, and engaging while creating experiences that feel unmistakably Spotify. \n Build interactive digital learning experiences using AI-assisted workflows and authoring tools such as Articulate Storyline or Rise, Adobe Captivate, or similar platforms. \n Design inclusive learning experiences that reflect different perspectives, reduce barriers to participation, and support a culture of belonging. \n Pilot and iterate on learning experiences using learner feedback, stakeholder input, and performance data. \n Define meaningful measures of success and evaluate learning effectiveness, knowledge transfer, learner experience, and behavior change. \n Manage multiple learning projects from initial scoping through delivery while creating clarity around priorities, timelines, and stakeholder expectations. \n Explore emerging approaches in learning design, including AI-assisted authoring and adaptive learning, and apply them where they can meaningfully improve the learner experience. \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n You have 5+ years of professional instructional design experience and a portfolio demonstrating thoughtful work across multiple learning formats. \n You apply learning science principles such as cognitive load, retrieval practice, spaced learning, and adult learning theory to practical design decisions. \n You know how to uncover learning and performance needs, translate them into measurable objectives, and design learning journeys that build knowledge and skills over time. \n You create meaningful practice through scenarios, simulations, assessments, and other interactive experiences rather than relying on passive content. \n You have strong visual and UX design judgment and understand how typography, hierarchy, layout, and visual storytelling can make learning clearer and easier to navigate. \n You have experience with rapid authoring tools such as Articulate 360, Captivate, Lectora, or similar platforms, along with design tools such as Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, or equivalent. \n You can create clear storyboards, scripts, facilitator guides, and supporting materials that help others confidently deliver consistent learning experiences. \n You use learner feedback and data to evaluate effectiveness, iterate on your work, and connect learning experiences to meaningful outcomes. \n You communicate complex ideas clearly and collaborate effectively with subject-matter experts, leaders, and cross-functional partners. \n You\u2019re comfortable navigating ambiguity, balancing multiple priorities, and taking ownership from an early idea through a polished learning experience. \n You bring experience in areas such as inclusive learning design, leadership development, learning technology, short-form learning video or animation, LMS/LXP platforms, or SCORM/xAPI. \n You have a degree in instructional design, learning sciences, education, human-computer interaction, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n This role is based in London or Stockholm \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nSenior Digital Learning Experience Designer, Learning & Inclusion\nGB\nhybrid\n\n\n \n We\u2019re looking for a Senior Digital Learning Experience Designer to join our Learning & Inclusion team, the group responsible for creating learning experiences that help every Spotify band member grow, belong, and do their best work. \n You\u2019ll bring together instructional design, visual design, storytelling, and broader learning and development expertise to create inclusive and effective experiences at scale. You\u2019ll partner with subject-matter experts, people leaders, and Learning & Inclusion colleagues on company-wide initiatives, from leadership development to programs that bring Spotify\u2019s values to life. \n \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/7cf725bb-99c8-4717-b7e5-4f4708fa4169\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/7cf725bb-99c8-4717-b7e5-4f4708fa4169/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n \n \n The United States base range for this position is $94,000 - $134,000, plus equity. The benefits available for this position include health insurance, six-month paid parental leave, 401(k) retirement plan, monthly meal allowance, 23 paid days off, 13 paid flexible holidays, paid sick leave. These ranges may be modified in the future. \n \n Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nPermanent\nContent\nLos Angeles, CA\nPodcast Business\nLos Angeles, CA\n\n Spotify is looking for a creative, strategic, and sharp editorial voice to join the US Podcast Editorial team. In this role, you'll lead high-visibility editorial projects end to end, partner cross-functionally as a creative and content expert, and shape how listeners discover and engage with podcasts and emerging formats on Spotify. The ideal candidate is a strong writer with a distinct editorial point of view who operates with independence and thrives at the intersection of creative judgment and platform strategy. This role reports into the Associate Director, Podcast Editorial & Audience Development. \n53c07681-f798-4f2c-bef6-513c6d027c9e\nWhat You'll Do\n\n Drive and lead strategic editorial projects from brief through execution and results, including tentpole programming, format testing, and seasonal initiatives \n Write compelling editorial copy and commentary that brings Spotify's editorial voice to life across curated surfaces and promotional moments \n Partner cross-functionally as a creative and content expert across workstreams spanning product, personalization, and marketing \n Own curation of high-complexity or high-visibility editorial surfaces, maintaining quality, cultural relevance, and freshness \n Collaborate with Partnerships to develop strategies that grow creator audiences on platform \n Represent Editorial's perspective in cross-functional working groups and planning conversations \n Identify cultural moments, content trends, and audience opportunities that can be translated into compelling programming across audio and video formats \n Collaborate with data and analytics teams to inform editorial strategy and measure impact \n\nWho You Are\n \n\n 5+ years of experience in editorial, content strategy, or audience development within media, digital, or audio \n An exceptional writer and editor with a sharp voice and the ability to craft copy that resonates with diverse audiences \n A strong editorial point of view paired with the ability to translate creative instincts into strategic plans \n Proven ability to lead complex projects independently and drive them to measurable outcomes \n Skilled cross-functional collaborator who can partner effectively with product, marketing, and technical teams \n Deep knowledge of the podcast and audio/video landscape, including creators, publishers, formats, and audience trends \n Curious and proactive about emerging tools and technology, including AI, and how they can amplify editorial work \n Comfortable working with data to inform decisions and demonstrate editorial impact \n A sharp cultural antenna with genuine enthusiasm for connecting audiences with voices and content they'll love \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n\n This role is based in Los Angeles. \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n We ask that you come into the office 2\u20133 days per week. \n\nSenior Editor, Podcast Editorial\nUS\nhybrid\n\n\n Spotify is looking for a creative, strategic, and sharp editorial voice to join the US Podcast Editorial team. In this role, you'll lead high-visibility editorial projects end to end, partner cross-functionally as a creative and content expert, and shape how listeners discover and engage with podcasts and emerging formats on Spotify. The ideal candidate is a strong writer with a distinct editorial point of view who operates with independence and thrives at the intersection of creative judgment and platform strategy. This role reports into the Associate Director, Podcast Editorial & Audience Development. \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/53c07681-f798-4f2c-bef6-513c6d027c9e\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/53c07681-f798-4f2c-bef6-513c6d027c9e/apply"}, "return": {"value": 94000, "stated": true, "evidence": "$94,000 - $134,000"}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Permanent\nEngineering\nLondon\nIT and Network Engineering\nLondon\nStockholm\n\n The Platform team creates the technology that enables Spotify to learn quickly and scale easily, enabling rapid growth in our users and our business around the globe. Spanning many disciplines, we work to make the business work; creating the infrastructure, tooling, frameworks, and capabilities needed to welcome a billion customers. \n \u00a0 \n The IT Studio exists to remove the friction of work, unblocking Spotifiers anywhere, anytime, with simplicity and safety. We are the team behind the technology that approximately 8,000 Spotifiers rely on every day, spanning endpoint and device management, identity and access, networking and connectivity, IT service management and support, audio visual and meeting room technology, productivity and collaboration platforms, work management tooling, and the AI tools changing how everyone at Spotify works. Across 9 teams, we touch almost every part of how Spotify functions as a company. \n \u00a0 \n We\u2019re looking for an experienced engineering leader to lead a group of Engineering Managers and approximately 50 engineers and technicians across the studio. You\u2019ll set engineering strategy, strengthen the technical practices that help our teams operate at their best, and partner closely with product and studio leadership to balance engineering investment with business priorities. \nc114627b-1306-4581-95a8-77d847ee9962\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n Lead and develop Engineering Managers across multiple teams, supporting their growth while creating clarity around outcomes and engineering excellence. \n Set and communicate engineering strategy across the studio, ensuring teams have clear technical direction aligned with IT\u2019s mandate and Spotify\u2019s business needs. \n Strengthen technical judgment across the Engineering Manager group, challenging processes that no longer add value and creating more space for architecture, quality, and team capability. \n Identify patterns and opportunities across teams and drive improvements in engineering practice, operational health, reliability, and ways of working. \n Establish and evolve engineering best practices across the studio, helping teams share knowledge and consistently improve how we build and operate technology. \n Champion reliability, security, compliance, and privacy as fundamental parts of engineering decision-making. \n Shape how AI is used across the company, both through the tools our squads build and how our engineers work day to day. \n Partner with studio and alliance leadership, procurement, legal, engineering counterparts, and teams across Spotify to make thoughtful technical investments and solve meaningful business problems. \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n You have 8+ years of engineering experience and experience leading Engineering Managers across multiple teams. \n You have led engineering organisations at scale and can demonstrate how the technical strategies you\u2019ve shaped have influenced meaningful outcomes. \n You bring experience with enterprise technology such as identity and access, SaaS platforms, endpoint management, workplace technology, architecture, or related systems, and can engage credibly in technical decisions across these areas. \n You have improved engineering practices across multiple teams and know how to balance developer productivity, operational excellence, reliability, and sustainable technical investment. \n You have developed Engineering Managers into stronger leaders and can point to meaningful growth and progression within the teams you\u2019ve led. \n You\u2019re excited about how AI is changing the way people and engineering organisations work and have practical experience applying AI tooling or related technologies. \n You focus performance conversations on impact rather than activity and can assess contributions across teams producing different kinds of outcomes. \n You\u2019re a strategic thinker who can set direction across a broad organisation while staying close enough to the work to contribute when needed. \n You communicate complex technical and strategic ideas clearly, build inclusion into how you lead, and can make thoughtful decisions when working through ambiguity. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n This role is based in London or Stockholm. \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nSenior Engineering Manager - Information Technology\nGB\nhybrid\n\n\n The Platform team creates the technology that enables Spotify to learn quickly and scale easily, enabling rapid growth in our users and our business around the globe. Spanning many disciplines, we work to make the business work; creating the infrastructure, tooling, frameworks, and capabilities needed to welcome a billion customers. \n \u00a0 \n The IT Studio exists to remove the friction of work, unblocking Spotifiers anywhere, anytime, with simplicity and safety. We are the team behind the technology that approximately 8,000 Spotifiers rely on every day, spanning endpoint and device management, identity and access, networking and connectivity, IT service management and support, audio visual and meeting room technology, productivity and collaboration platforms, work management tooling, and the AI tools changing how everyone at Spotify works. Across 9 teams, we touch almost every part of how Spotify functions as a company. \n \u00a0 \n We\u2019re looking for an experienced engineering leader to lead a group of Engineering Managers and approximately 50 engineers and technicians across the studio. You\u2019ll set engineering strategy, strengthen the technical practices that help our teams operate at their best, and partner closely with product and studio leadership to balance engineering investment with business priorities. \n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/c114627b-1306-4581-95a8-77d847ee9962\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/c114627b-1306-4581-95a8-77d847ee9962/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
{"caller": "infer_field_from_text__n13", "instruction": "You are given the plain text of a single job posting and the name of one field. Determine that field's value as stated by this posting text, and nothing else.\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly these three keys:\n  value    - the field's value as the text states it, or null if the text does not state it\n  stated   - true only if the posting text states this field; false otherwise\n  evidence - the shortest verbatim substring of the posting text that states the value, or null when stated is false\n\nRules: never infer a value the text does not support; when the text is silent about the field, stated must be false and value must be null. When stated is true, evidence must appear verbatim in the posting text. Return the JSON object and nothing else.", "payload": {"field": "salary_floor", "posting_text": "Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens.\n\u00a0\nAt Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can.\n\u00a0\n\n Spotify is an equal opportunity employer. You are welcome at Spotify for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or what\u2019s playing in your headphones. Our platform is for everyone, and so is our workplace. The more voices we have represented and amplified in our business, the more we will all thrive, contribute, and be forward-thinking! So bring us your personal experience, your perspectives, and your background. It\u2019s in our differences that we will find the power to keep revolutionizing the way the world listens. \n \u00a0 \n At Spotify, we are passionate about inclusivity and making sure our entire recruitment process is accessible to everyone. We have ways to request reasonable accommodations during the interview process and help assist in what you need. If you need accommodations at any stage of the application or interview process, please let us know - we\u2019re here to support you in any way we can. \n \u00a0 \nEngineering\nLondon\nExperience\nLondon\nStockholm\nContent Platform is responsible for ingesting, processing, storing, and delivering every piece of content on Spotify \u2014 from music and podcasts to audiobooks. Within Content Platform, the Media domain owns the end-to-end media pipeline, from the moment content arrives through to seamless playback for listeners around the world. We're looking for a Staff Engineer to provide architectural leadership across this media platform. You\u2019ll help shape and drive the technical direction from ingestion through transcoding, packaging, storage, delivery, and playback. This is a role for someone who thinks in systems, understands the trade-offs between codec choices and infrastructure costs, and can drive technical strategy across multiple teams at scale.\n\n Content Platform is responsible for ingesting, processing, storing, and delivering every piece of content on Spotify \u2014 from music and podcasts to audiobooks. Within Content Platform, the Media domain owns the end-to-end media pipeline, from the moment content arrives through to seamless playback for listeners around the world. We're looking for a Staff Engineer to provide architectural leadership across this media platform. You\u2019ll help shape and drive the technical direction from ingestion through transcoding, packaging, storage, delivery, and playback. This is a role for someone who thinks in systems, understands the trade-offs between codec choices and infrastructure costs, and can drive technical strategy across multiple teams at scale. \nbe2d7d1e-939e-47f9-8db7-278caa101a60\nWhat You'll Do\n \n\n Define and drive the long-term architectural direction for Spotify's media pipeline across Content Platform. \n Lead large-scale technical initiatives that span multiple squads and organizations, including projects such as media delivery, codec rollouts, and future playback capabilities. \n Partner closely with engineering managers, product managers, and senior engineers to align technical strategy with product priorities, reliability goals, and cost efficiency, acting as a key technical counterpart for media architecture. \n Guide architectural decisions across media ingestion, transcoding, packaging, storage, content delivery, and playback. \n Author and review RFCs, architecture decision records, and technical design documents that guide engineering teams and leadership. \n Mentor senior engineers across the organization, helping raise technical quality, architectural thinking, and engineering excellence. \n Bring a cost-aware engineering mindset by understanding how media architecture decisions impact compute, storage, CDN utilization, and long-term platform sustainability. \n\n \nWho You Are\n \n\n You have deep expertise building large-scale media platforms spanning audio, video, encoding, transcoding, packaging, delivery, and playback technologies. \n You have successfully led architecture across multiple engineering teams and influenced technical direction beyond your immediate organization. \n You have significant experience designing and operating distributed systems at internet scale, including high-throughput media processing, large-scale storage, and globally distributed delivery infrastructure. \n You understand the architectural trade-offs between codecs, packaging formats, playback technologies, storage, networking, and infrastructure costs. \n You have a strong track record of leading multi-quarter technical initiatives from initial proposal through implementation and organization-wide adoption. \n You communicate technical ideas clearly through well-structured RFCs, design documents, and architectural decision records. \n You build trust through collaboration and technical credibility, bringing together teams with different priorities to deliver shared outcomes. \n You enjoy mentoring experienced engineers and helping organizations grow their technical capability. \n Experience working with cloud infrastructure providers, CDN vendors, and large-scale media delivery ecosystems is highly valued. \n\n \nWhere You'll Be\n \n\n This role is based in London or Stockholm \n We offer you the flexibility to work where you work best! There will be some in person meetings, but still allows for flexibility to work from home. \n\n \nStaff Engineer - Content Platform\nGB\nhybrid\n\n\n Content Platform is responsible for ingesting, processing, storing, and delivering every piece of content on Spotify \u2014 from music and podcasts to audiobooks. Within Content Platform, the Media domain owns the end-to-end media pipeline, from the moment content arrives through to seamless playback for listeners around the world. We're looking for a Staff Engineer to provide architectural leadership across this media platform. You\u2019ll help shape and drive the technical direction from ingestion through transcoding, packaging, storage, delivery, and playback. This is a role for someone who thinks in systems, understands the trade-offs between codec choices and infrastructure costs, and can drive technical strategy across multiple teams at scale. \nContent Platform is responsible for ingesting, processing, storing, and delivering every piece of content on Spotify \u2014 from music and podcasts to audiobooks. Within Content Platform, the Media domain owns the end-to-end media pipeline, from the moment content arrives through to seamless playback for listeners around the world. We're looking for a Staff Engineer to provide architectural leadership across this media platform. You\u2019ll help shape and drive the technical direction from ingestion through transcoding, packaging, storage, delivery, and playback. This is a role for someone who thinks in systems, understands the trade-offs between codec choices and infrastructure costs, and can drive technical strategy across multiple teams at scale.\n\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/be2d7d1e-939e-47f9-8db7-278caa101a60\nhttps://jobs.lever.co/spotify/be2d7d1e-939e-47f9-8db7-278caa101a60/apply"}, "return": {"value": null, "stated": false, "evidence": null}}
